# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots apache2 serving the vulnerable WordPress tree and
# then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the web server is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, so verify.sh can
#     hold the agent responsible for keeping it alive instead of starting it;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting Apache cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Note: DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT lives in wp-config.php, which PHP re-reads on every
# request, so this particular fix does not require an Apache restart - but a
# STOPPED or broken Apache is now a hard FAILURE rather than something verify.sh
# quietly repairs.
